Lumen OS, XGIMI Play 6 only: software keystone in SurfaceFlinger, as the stock XGIMI SurfaceFlinger did.

The vendor trapezoidServer publishes the keystone corners as vendor.mstar.pos_*_offset and bumps
vendor.mstar.trapezoid.trigger.osd.offset; the vendor HWC then asks for a refresh. The stock (Android 11)
SurfaceFlinger warped the client target with them (GLESTrapezoidalRenderEngine). This patch adds the
corner quad to DisplaySettings (so the client composition cache misses on a change), fills it for physical
displays in CompositionEngine Display, and applies a 4-point perspective transform in SkiaRenderEngine.
Quality as stock (2026-10-29, owner's tester saw stair-steps): the stock GLESTrapezoidalRenderEngine
sampled every layer with GL_LINEAR and drew into a 4x MSAA target; here every buffer layer is sampled
linear while the keystone is on, rectangular layers get edge anti-aliasing, and the client target is
rendered with 4x MSAA like stock (AutoBackendTexture, GL_EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture on the
Mali-G52, falls back to no MSAA if the driver refuses).
Research: docs/play6/research/keystone_stock.md. Applied only to the Play 6 base build (play6_overrides.sh).

